A||||3||Shinerdc||Help replacement head options||||1||
Z||000000||Shinerdc||11-21-2001||10:46 PM||||have an 84 2.5l and ends up the head is cracked....could be stitched but machine shop says not a good option...one message said an s10 head would do....looking for info from the knowledge base...please and thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-22-2001||02:39 AM||||I've had an S-10 head on my '84 for the last couple of years.  Havn't had any problems at all, and the car ran 185 degrees last month at Sebring on a 77 degree day.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||11-22-2001||09:12 AM||||I used the head from a 2.5 out of a 79 Monza.  It has the plain oval combustion chambers.  I believe you can use about any 2.5 head that calls for the same head gasket as the Fiero head.  You may have to transfer the freeze plugs(inner and outer) and the thermostat housing from one end to the other as I did.  Had to grind away about 1/4 inch of the bottom bolt hole flange on the thermostat housing, but other than those items, it was a direct bolt on.<P>Hope you find one soon.<BR>Forgot to mention, this head has been in service 5 years and 15,000 miles with no problems whatsoever.<BR>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ITB 2M4||11-23-2001||12:42 AM||||Yeah, I kinda forgot to mention that the filler neck for the thermostat is on the opposite end of the head, but all you have to do it swap the neck and freeze plug around.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
